    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your high-density racking in Rotterdam, managing the center of gravity is crucial; you want to keep the load as low and centered as possible, especially with heavy industrial goods. Think about a very wide, low-slung stack of the most massive components, like a very sturdy, low-level base layer. If you're stacking crates, ensure the weight distribution across each pallet is even, and consider using load-bearing dunnage or interlocking patterns that distribute the weight evenly across the supporting pallet structure. These techniques will significantly boost stability against tipping.",
