    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, absolutely, external vibrations and forklift handling are major culprits for sudden shifts, even if the load *looks* fine one moment. When a forklift moves too aggressively, or if the warehouse experiences heavy vibrations from nearby machinery or even passing trucks, it can induce dynamic forces on the stack. This is like a small, persistent tremor that slowly encourages the load to settle into an unstable configuration. You need to train your drivers to move with the utmost gentleness, especially when approaching or leaving a high stack.",
      "source": "target",
